    crgo:CRGO_0000252 "An attacker in or near a clinic exploits weak wireless security, an unsegmented guest network or a rogue access point to join the clinic network, intercept credentials and reach EHR workstations and local storage."@en ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000253 "A pre-shared Wi-Fi key posted in a staff room is reused on the guest network, which routes to the clinic LAN. An attacker in the waiting room scans the network, finds a file share on the local storage unit and a workstation with an open remote desktop service."@en ;
